<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles III of Navarre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1361–1425</span> · Also known as Charles III the Noble</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles III the Noble was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a> from 1387, of the French house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evreux">Évreux</a>. Unlike his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-ii-of-navarre">Charles the Bad</a>, he kept peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, exchanging his Norman claims for the duchy of Nemours. He reorganised the kingdom's administration, united the boroughs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pamplona">Pamplona</a> in 1423, and built the palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olite">Olite</a> and the cathedral cloister of Pamplona.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-iii-of-navarre.jpg" alt="Charles III of Navarre" width="320" height="508" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karel3_Evreux_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
